## Self-review, cleanup, and limitations

Reviewed the focused diff for exact-path call coverage, raw-edge handling, pending-authority forwarding, canonical LF mount paths, identity binding, pin lifetime, partial materialization, cleanup ordering, and preservation of manifest/parent bytes. No unrelated source refactor was introduced.

Owned scratch cleanup completed after a resolved absolute path check against this exact worktree using `Remove-Item -LiteralPath $ownedScratch -Recurse -Force`; only `.baseline-fix-scratch` was removed. The command verified absence afterward and printed `Owned synthetic scratch removed; containment verified` with exit 0. Final `git status --short` showed only the controller's modified `progress.md`; the index was empty and `git diff --check` passed. The durable brief and this report remain in place and unstaged (ignored by Git). No source bytecode was generated by the direct runs.

This is source-first verification. It does not certify an actual evaluator image, real baseline capture, real panels or bundles, market results, or production Docker behavior. Complete successful baseline capture/repeat semantics remain those of the original implementation; the repair directly exercised graph failure boundaries, successful graph/profile composition, panel loading failure, and real transport overlay composition with synthetic fakes. No tests, provider/network calls, Docker actions, replay, confirmation, qualification, worktree materialization, push, merge, uploads, or improved-return claims were made.
